  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Two identical uniform discs roll without slipping on two different surfaces <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></math> (see figure) starting at <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> with linear speeds <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">υ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">υ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> , respectively, and always remain in contact with the surfaces. If they reach <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></math> with the same linear speed and <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">υ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi></math> m/s, then <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">υ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> in m/s is <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math><br ><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/image5-4c0aca5f-f276-4e40-b0c6-ce9b5bb384d0.png\"/></p>",
    "image": null
  },
